00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:05,530
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,611 --> 00:00:10,449
9 YEARS LATER
THE BLUE HOUSE, 1979

2
00:00:10,532 --> 00:00:12,534
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

3
00:00:20,792 --> 00:00:22,169
[President Park] Deputy Director Baek.

4
00:00:22,711 --> 00:00:23,712
Hello, sir.

5
00:00:24,379 --> 00:00:26,173
That's right. I'm Baek Kitae.

6
00:00:26,256 --> 00:00:28,925
The deputy director of
the Korean Central Intelligence Agency.

7
00:00:30,844 --> 00:00:32,596
So… [sighs]

8
00:00:34,723 --> 00:00:36,767
…how long have I been in this chair?

9
00:00:37,476 --> 00:00:39,561
Almost… two decades.

10
00:00:40,896 --> 00:00:44,399
And that's far too long for this job,
isn't it?

11
00:00:44,483 --> 00:00:45,984
Absolutely not.

12
00:00:46,068 --> 00:00:47,235
[chuckles] Yes, it is.

13
00:00:48,445 --> 00:00:51,365
That's why there's been such a…
strident outcry.

14
00:00:51,448 --> 00:00:53,325
Don't worry about that.

15
00:00:53,408 --> 00:00:56,036
People love to raise their voices.
They'll all stop soon.

16
00:01:00,916 --> 00:01:02,417
On a separate subject,

17
00:01:02,501 --> 00:01:05,754
the way Director Cho's been
looking at me lately, well…

18
00:01:06,963 --> 00:01:08,340
it's different now.

19
00:01:08,965 --> 00:01:11,009
What's your opinion? You agree?

20
00:01:12,386 --> 00:01:14,429
Busan's dealing with the protests.

21
00:01:14,513 --> 00:01:16,682
I'd say that's putting him
in a tough position.

22
00:01:16,765 --> 00:01:18,600
President Park's left and right hands:

23
00:01:18,684 --> 00:01:23,188
Director Cho of the KCIA and Chief Gwak
of the Presidential Security Service.

24
00:01:23,271 --> 00:01:27,401
On the surface, they claim to be searching
for a solution to the unrest in Busan.

25
00:01:28,151 --> 00:01:30,946
But the truth is they're competing
for the president's favor

26
00:01:31,029 --> 00:01:32,864
and their share of the pie.

27
00:01:32,948 --> 00:01:35,492
The Yushin regime is autocratic
and tyrannical.

28
00:01:37,744 --> 00:01:39,705
That's what all the protestors are saying.

29
00:01:40,455 --> 00:01:43,166
[Kitae] And then there's Cheon Seokjung,
Park's Chief of Staff,

30
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:45,710
and the second-most powerful man
in the country right now.

31
00:01:45,794 --> 00:01:48,004
Look, I'm sure they have their reasons.

32
00:01:48,839 --> 00:01:49,923
What?

33
00:01:50,006 --> 00:01:54,302
Things will only get worse if we decide
to suppress the demonstrations by force.

34
00:01:54,386 --> 00:01:58,432
See what I mean? The KCIA has
gone too damn soft for my taste.

35
00:01:58,515 --> 00:02:01,810
It's giving these commie protestors
whatever they want.

36
00:02:02,394 --> 00:02:04,729
I say let's just roll some tanks in there.

37
00:02:05,313 --> 00:02:07,524
And you, shut your mouth.

38
00:02:07,607 --> 00:02:10,527
What'd you say to me, you asshole? Huh?

39
00:02:10,610 --> 00:02:13,280
Come on, that's enough.
Don't be so vulgar.

40
00:02:13,363 --> 00:02:15,699
Oh, I think you heard me.

41
00:02:16,324 --> 00:02:17,743
Asshole!

42
00:02:18,243 --> 00:02:20,537
Hey, hey, cool it. Let's be civil here.

43
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:23,081
-You little shit.
-[Gwak chuckling] Whoa, here we go.

44
00:02:23,165 --> 00:02:25,375
-Have you lost your damn mind or what?
-Excuse me?

45
00:02:25,459 --> 00:02:27,961
You really want to push me over the line,
you asshole?

46
00:02:28,044 --> 00:02:29,755
You know, swearing won't fix the country.

47
00:02:29,838 --> 00:02:31,423
-[grunting] How dare you…
-[grunting]

48
00:02:31,506 --> 00:02:32,883
-I'm gonna crush you…
-[grunting]

49
00:02:32,966 --> 00:02:35,510
[Cho] Think you can get cocky
just 'cause the president's backing you?

50
00:02:35,594 --> 00:02:37,596
[Gwak] Think you're better than me,
you piece of shit?

51
00:02:38,555 --> 00:02:39,973
Cho's become too soft.

52
00:02:41,057 --> 00:02:43,310
The KCIA needs to crack down harder.

53
00:02:44,853 --> 00:02:47,105
-Don't you think?
-Absolutely, sir.

54
00:02:48,607 --> 00:02:50,442
Stick as close as you can to Cho.

55
00:02:50,525 --> 00:02:52,152
Keep an eye on him, my friend.

56
00:02:52,986 --> 00:02:54,488
-[knock on door]
-Yes, sir.

57
00:02:54,571 --> 00:02:55,572
[door opens]

58
00:02:59,117 --> 00:03:00,952
Mr. President, Madam Shin is here.

59
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:06,583
Ah, there you are.
Glad you could make it, Madam Shin.

60
00:03:10,629 --> 00:03:13,715
I was feeling a little unsettled
after a strange dream.

61
00:03:13,799 --> 00:03:14,800
[clicks tongue]

62
00:03:17,344 --> 00:03:20,096
By the way, this is Baek Kitae,
the man I told you about.

63
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:23,391
He's the deputy director of the KCIA.

64
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:26,520
Introduce yourself.

65
00:03:28,563 --> 00:03:29,814
Baek Kitae, madam.

66
00:03:32,859 --> 00:03:34,569
You're very handsome.

67
00:03:38,031 --> 00:03:39,407
I'm Madam Shin.

68
00:03:39,491 --> 00:03:41,493
[♪ intriguing music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

69
00:03:47,999 --> 00:03:50,669
You have such lovely hands too.

70
00:03:59,761 --> 00:04:04,558
[in Japanese] I can see why
you treasure him so dearly, sir.

71
00:04:06,768 --> 00:04:12,315
He'll lead this country
as the next KCIA director.

72
00:04:12,399 --> 00:04:14,651
[in English] At your service!
[in Japanese] Thank you!

73
00:04:15,443 --> 00:04:19,197
[in English] Oh, wow.
So you speak a little Japanese as well?

74
00:04:21,116 --> 00:04:23,076
I lived in Osaka for a while.

75
00:04:23,159 --> 00:04:25,662
Ah, Osaka.

76
00:04:26,329 --> 00:04:27,330
Very nice.

77
00:04:28,874 --> 00:04:32,794
All right, Baek, keep a close watch
on Cho and report to me regularly.

78
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:34,629
Of course, sir!

79
00:04:35,255 --> 00:04:38,091
I think it's time to go in, Madam Shin.

80
00:04:39,134 --> 00:04:40,302
'Cause I'm getting impatient.

81
00:04:41,636 --> 00:04:42,888
All right, let's go.

82
00:05:07,287 --> 00:05:09,331
[softly] So I'll be the director?

83
00:05:11,958 --> 00:05:13,001
[chuckles]

84
00:05:13,752 --> 00:05:15,253
[♪ theme music playing]

85
00:06:10,475 --> 00:06:12,811
[Cho] That son of a bitch
has gone insane, I swear.

86
00:06:12,894 --> 00:06:13,895
[door opens]

87
00:06:13,979 --> 00:06:16,272
[Cho] He's not gonna get away with this.
[breathing heavily]

88
00:06:16,356 --> 00:06:18,984
-Good afternoon, Director.
-Gonna smash his smug little face in.

89
00:06:20,193 --> 00:06:21,695
That bastard is dead.

90
00:06:21,778 --> 00:06:23,530
I'm gonna tear him to little pieces.

91
00:06:24,614 --> 00:06:25,699
What's the matter?

92
00:06:28,535 --> 00:06:30,870
Baek, listen. You trust me?

93
00:06:31,913 --> 00:06:33,581
Of course, sir, completely.

94
00:06:33,665 --> 00:06:36,126
Good. Trust only me.

95
00:06:36,209 --> 00:06:38,378
One day, I'll end all of this.

96
00:06:38,461 --> 00:06:40,422
That's the only way we'll survive.

97
00:06:41,339 --> 00:06:43,258
I don't know what you mean by that.

98
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:49,556
"Life's a long journey.
It's so easy to be led astray.

99
00:06:51,474 --> 00:06:53,852
But if a man's determined
to walk his path,

100
00:06:54,644 --> 00:06:56,896
any storm can be weathered.

101
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:58,690
He'll make his own way."

102
00:07:04,237 --> 00:07:05,488
Have a good day.

103
00:07:13,329 --> 00:07:15,540
[person] Ah, good aftern… What the…

104
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:21,546
Deputy Director Baek, good afternoon.

105
00:07:22,046 --> 00:07:26,134
[Kitae] Major General Hwang Daesik,
leader of the Military Security Command.

106
00:07:27,135 --> 00:07:30,096
He's known Cheon Seokjung,
the president's favorite advisor,

107
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:32,724
since their days
at the Korean Military Academy.

108
00:07:32,807 --> 00:07:36,811
But even so, Hwang's been gunning
for Cheon's position for a long time.
STYLE
::cue()

109
00:07:38,938 --> 00:07:40,690
Are you here for the president?

110
00:07:40,774 --> 00:07:42,567
I have something I need to report.

111
00:07:42,650 --> 00:07:45,111
[♪ intriguing music playing]

112
00:07:45,195 --> 00:07:46,529
Busan keeping you busy lately?

113
00:07:47,363 --> 00:07:51,367
Those bastards. They love to riot
like animals, that's all it is.

114
00:07:51,451 --> 00:07:54,829
After everything the president's done
to better this country,

115
00:07:55,413 --> 00:07:59,167
suddenly a bunch of ungrateful protestors
are whining about terms limits.

116
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:02,253
And no mention of Kim Ilsung
who's been making himself a god

117
00:08:02,337 --> 00:08:04,047
for the last 30 years. [clicks tongue]

118
00:08:04,756 --> 00:08:06,174
Democracy?

119
00:08:06,257 --> 00:08:08,885
Do these morons even know
what that word means?

120
00:08:08,968 --> 00:08:10,762
Pampered sons of bitches.

121
00:08:10,845 --> 00:08:14,182
Why don't we just round them up quick
and lop off their heads one by one?

122
00:08:17,143 --> 00:08:19,062
Why don't you and I get a drink sometime?

123
00:08:20,063 --> 00:08:21,481
Why not tonight?

124
00:08:21,564 --> 00:08:23,358
First round's on me.

125
00:08:23,983 --> 00:08:27,612
-Sorry, tonight is no good.
-Ah. [laughs]

126
00:08:28,655 --> 00:08:30,114
Well, I'm gonna hold you to it.

127
00:08:32,826 --> 00:08:35,578
I'll see you around, Mr. Baek. [chuckles]

128
00:08:42,335 --> 00:08:45,213
[sighing] That little bastard.
I should just…

129
00:08:50,802 --> 00:08:51,803
Geez.

130
00:08:53,304 --> 00:08:55,807
Hwang Daesik went
to the president's office?

131
00:08:57,058 --> 00:08:59,853
Yes. It seems the president's been
taking an interest in him lately.

132
00:08:59,936 --> 00:09:01,646
CHIEF OF STAFF TO THE PRESIDENT
CHEON SEOKJUNG

133
00:09:01,729 --> 00:09:03,439
Inviting him to drinks and all that.

134
00:09:03,523 --> 00:09:05,525
Wow, that jackass.

135
00:09:09,362 --> 00:09:10,738
Baek, I think… [sighs]

136
00:09:12,198 --> 00:09:14,492
…we should teach that prick
a lesson while we can.

137
00:09:16,578 --> 00:09:17,996
What do you have in mind?

138
00:09:19,289 --> 00:09:20,874
Why don't you come up with something?

139
00:09:21,916 --> 00:09:23,668
We need to humble him…

140
00:09:24,460 --> 00:09:26,880
before he gets too big for his britches.

141
00:09:27,505 --> 00:09:30,550
[Kitae] Chief Cheon has wielded
absolute power for over a decade,

142
00:09:30,633 --> 00:09:34,554
but even so, he's always
playing second fiddle to the president.

143
00:09:34,637 --> 00:09:36,723
By the way… [sighs]

144
00:09:36,806 --> 00:09:38,933
…you know how disappointed
the president was

145
00:09:39,017 --> 00:09:40,226
with the last election, right?

146
00:09:41,477 --> 00:09:43,688
Are you talking about the campaign funds?

147
00:09:43,771 --> 00:09:44,772
[lighter flicks open]

148
00:09:46,774 --> 00:09:50,320
This time we need to make sure
we have a sizeable war chest.

149
00:09:51,779 --> 00:09:55,700
Sir, I gathered all the resources
I could back then.

150
00:09:55,783 --> 00:09:56,993
Kitae, listen.

151
00:09:58,286 --> 00:10:00,538
I'm not making this request
out of self-interest.

152
00:10:00,622 --> 00:10:01,915
[Kitae sighs]

153
00:10:01,998 --> 00:10:05,335
This is all about
planting enough allies, all right?

154
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:10,298
We need people
in the National Assembly. Hey.

155
00:10:12,967 --> 00:10:15,637
You know why the president
favors Daesik these days?

156
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,555
[Kitae exhales deeply]

157
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:20,808
He tests your loyalty from time to time,
that much I know.

158
00:10:22,101 --> 00:10:23,436
So maybe…

159
00:10:23,519 --> 00:10:26,439
he's trying to toughen you up
and make your skin thicker

160
00:10:27,315 --> 00:10:29,359
before he steps down
and hands his seat to you.

161
00:10:29,442 --> 00:10:32,111
[laughing]

162
00:10:35,823 --> 00:10:39,160
Kitae, Kitae…

163
00:10:42,288 --> 00:10:44,582
You still don't know him at all.

164
00:10:46,459 --> 00:10:50,672
That man has absolutely
no intention of stepping down. Ever.

165
00:10:52,590 --> 00:10:53,925
Don't you get it?

166
00:10:56,344 --> 00:10:57,845
It's because of me.

167
00:10:57,929 --> 00:11:01,516
He's got Hwang Daesik
glued to his hip to keep me in check.

168
00:11:04,227 --> 00:11:05,979
His time's running out, though.

169
00:11:09,148 --> 00:11:11,025
He's not as sharp as he was.
STYLE
::cue()

170
00:11:14,612 --> 00:11:16,239
[car horns honking]

171
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:20,827
[♪ classical music playing on stereo]

172
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:22,161
Tell me, Kihun.

173
00:11:22,829 --> 00:11:23,913
[Kihun] Yes, sir.

174
00:11:25,206 --> 00:11:27,250
You've been working with me how long now?

175
00:11:27,917 --> 00:11:30,211
Seven or eight years, I think?

176
00:11:31,546 --> 00:11:33,214
Ever since you moved to Seoul.

177
00:11:34,132 --> 00:11:36,676
Your accent's just as obvious
as it was then.

178
00:11:37,510 --> 00:11:40,388
[Kihun] I've been doing my best, sir.
Is it that easy to tell?

179
00:11:41,431 --> 00:11:43,224
I mean, what do you think?

180
00:11:43,308 --> 00:11:44,892
I'm sorry, sir. I'll try harder.

181
00:11:45,768 --> 00:11:47,228
That's not why I asked.

182
00:11:49,063 --> 00:11:51,232
When do the materials from Taiwan arrive?

183
00:11:51,316 --> 00:11:52,859
Should be here by Sunday, sir.

184
00:11:55,069 --> 00:11:56,863
[Kitae] Make sure to run the lab
day and night

185
00:11:56,946 --> 00:11:58,656
to hit the volume we need.

186
00:11:58,740 --> 00:11:59,949
[Kihun] Understood.

187
00:12:04,370 --> 00:12:05,538
By the way, sir,

188
00:12:06,497 --> 00:12:10,710
do you mind if…
I ask you something about the business?

189
00:12:11,377 --> 00:12:12,462
What is it?

190
00:12:12,545 --> 00:12:14,255
Well, wouldn't we…

191
00:12:15,006 --> 00:12:16,924
wouldn't we increase profits…

192
00:12:17,467 --> 00:12:19,719
if we sold our product here in Korea too?

193
00:12:21,304 --> 00:12:23,222
Exports are important,
but the local market--

194
00:12:23,306 --> 00:12:25,641
-Kihun.
-Uh, yes, sir?

195
00:12:26,392 --> 00:12:29,687
If you don't want to die,
focus on driving.

196
00:12:31,105 --> 00:12:32,231
Yes, I apologize.

197
00:12:37,945 --> 00:12:40,740
Why would we push drugs
in this beautiful country?

198
00:12:41,699 --> 00:12:42,992
Don't forget…

199
00:12:45,286 --> 00:12:47,413
what we do is for patriotism.

200
00:12:47,497 --> 00:12:48,664
For our nation.

201
00:12:48,748 --> 00:12:50,625
Yes, of course. Our nation.

202
00:12:55,296 --> 00:12:56,547
[Kitae sighs]

203
00:13:00,093 --> 00:13:01,677
What a gorgeous day.

204
00:13:04,430 --> 00:13:06,724
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

205
00:13:26,452 --> 00:13:28,788
-[forklift beeping]
-[whistle blowing]

206
00:13:36,379 --> 00:13:38,339
[vocalizing]

207
00:13:38,423 --> 00:13:40,758
[scatting]

208
00:13:40,842 --> 00:13:43,636
Well, well, well. Here we are.
That was quick.

209
00:13:44,679 --> 00:13:46,848
[worker] Bring it this way! More, more.

210
00:13:46,931 --> 00:13:48,808
-Changbae.
-Yeah?

211
00:13:49,308 --> 00:13:51,435
Can you hear the sound
of money rolling in?

212
00:13:52,061 --> 00:13:54,188
[Changbae] Oh, yeah.
I hear it loud and clear.

213
00:13:54,856 --> 00:13:57,650
-Pick up the pace! Move it!
-[chuckles]

214
00:13:58,401 --> 00:14:01,654
OSAKA, JAPAN

215
00:14:03,114 --> 00:14:05,158
[Ikeda, in Japanese] Thank you for coming.

216
00:14:05,241 --> 00:14:09,537
There's one simple reason
I called you all here today.

217
00:14:11,038 --> 00:14:13,166
As you all know by now…

218
00:14:14,917 --> 00:14:17,628
my health is failing rather quickly.

219
00:14:18,754 --> 00:14:20,173
Which means that…

220
00:14:21,007 --> 00:14:24,135
remaining in this position
would only reflect…

221
00:14:25,386 --> 00:14:27,221
my own arrogance.

222
00:14:27,930 --> 00:14:28,931
No…

223
00:14:30,641 --> 00:14:33,978
More like excessive greed on my part.

224
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:35,938
Please, Kumicho.

225
00:14:36,856 --> 00:14:38,858
I urge you to reconsider.
STYLE
::cue()

226
00:14:40,026 --> 00:14:41,736
[all] Please reconsider!

227
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:45,698
[Kitae, in Korean] Choi Yuji has been
biding her time with her head down

228
00:14:45,781 --> 00:14:47,742
and her claws retracted.

229
00:14:47,825 --> 00:14:49,911
She's waited a while for this moment.

230
00:14:50,703 --> 00:14:52,205
[in Japanese] The Ikeda clan…

231
00:14:53,789 --> 00:14:57,460
must not take its current prosperity
for granted.

232
00:14:58,169 --> 00:14:59,879
No complacency.

233
00:15:03,633 --> 00:15:05,718
We must keep rebuilding…

234
00:15:06,969 --> 00:15:11,224
through strong reforms
that bolster the foundation we built.

235
00:15:11,307 --> 00:15:13,267
At the next general meeting,

236
00:15:13,351 --> 00:15:15,770
I will announce my successor,

237
00:15:16,771 --> 00:15:19,398
and my decision will be final.

238
00:15:20,691 --> 00:15:23,402
[Kitae, in Korean] But no matter
how shrewd and capable she is,

239
00:15:23,486 --> 00:15:26,656
clan leadership would
never willingly accept

240
00:15:26,739 --> 00:15:30,159
a young female Zainichi
as the official successor.

241
00:15:31,035 --> 00:15:32,328
[Kimura, in Japanese] Understood, sir.

242
00:15:33,287 --> 00:15:35,957
If that's what our kumicho
intends for the future…

243
00:15:37,458 --> 00:15:40,086
we will follow you and obey your will.

244
00:15:40,670 --> 00:15:42,338
[all, in Japanese] We will follow it!

245
00:15:43,506 --> 00:15:46,717
[Kitae, in Korean] If she has any hope
of claiming that seat and rising to power,

246
00:15:46,801 --> 00:15:50,554
her first step is to overcome
this man: Kimura Yoichi.

247
00:15:54,433 --> 00:15:55,851
[Harimoto, in Japanese]
You wanted to talk?

248
00:15:55,935 --> 00:15:57,478
[Yuji] I'll get straight to the point.

249
00:15:58,479 --> 00:16:01,399
I want your assistance
with the succession, Harimoto.

250
00:16:02,316 --> 00:16:03,317
[Harimoto scoffs]

251
00:16:03,401 --> 00:16:05,778
Kimura's conservative and old-fashioned.

252
00:16:05,861 --> 00:16:09,740
Under him, the clan will stagnate.
Who knows, it may even wither away.

253
00:16:11,075 --> 00:16:12,702
You know that, don't you?

254
00:16:14,412 --> 00:16:15,913
Well, the fact remains.

255
00:16:16,497 --> 00:16:19,667
It's very possible
that your father will choose him.

256
00:16:20,376 --> 00:16:21,836
[bird chirping]

257
00:16:21,919 --> 00:16:23,754
[Yuji] Don't worry. Leave that to me.

258
00:16:24,463 --> 00:16:28,509
The real question is,
what happens in a power vacuum?

259
00:16:30,594 --> 00:16:33,264
Harimoto, if you and I were
to collaborate,

260
00:16:34,015 --> 00:16:35,933
don't you think we might prevail?

261
00:16:37,685 --> 00:16:38,894
[sighs]

262
00:16:42,356 --> 00:16:46,944
[in Korean] I heard your brother was
arrested in Korea for foreign espionage.

263
00:16:48,738 --> 00:16:51,574
You know I have ties
with the KCIA, don't you?

264
00:16:52,783 --> 00:16:56,329
If you want… I'll make sure he gets out.

265
00:16:59,665 --> 00:17:02,668
In Korea, espionage
gets you the death penalty.

266
00:17:04,337 --> 00:17:08,507
So, then, will you really take over
this clan as kumicho?

267
00:17:10,092 --> 00:17:11,510
[chuckling]

268
00:17:15,931 --> 00:17:19,310
[Kitae] Yuji's lifelong dream has
been to lead the clan as kumicho.

269
00:17:20,770 --> 00:17:23,147
She'd do anything to be in control.

270
00:17:25,483 --> 00:17:27,902
Professor Jang Gyeongsik?

271
00:17:27,985 --> 00:17:30,446
[Yuji] He's the brother
of our regional boss, Harimoto.

272
00:17:31,155 --> 00:17:32,948
I mentioned him before, right?

273
00:17:33,949 --> 00:17:35,660
He runs our Tokyo operation.

274
00:17:37,036 --> 00:17:38,954
He's a Zainichi, like me.

275
00:17:40,122 --> 00:17:42,750
Kimura's one of the old guard,
from the main family…

276
00:17:43,709 --> 00:17:46,003
but Harimoto would be a big help to me.

277
00:17:46,087 --> 00:17:47,838
Kimura could be swayed by that.

278
00:17:48,464 --> 00:17:50,966
After all, Harimoto has
a major stake in the clan,

279
00:17:51,050 --> 00:17:52,635
and his influence runs deep.

280
00:17:52,718 --> 00:17:54,762
What exactly do you need from me, then?

281
00:17:54,845 --> 00:17:56,347
[bird chirping]

282
00:17:57,348 --> 00:18:01,686
Professor Jang Gyeongsik went
to Korea to visit his ancestral graves,

283
00:18:01,769 --> 00:18:03,396
and got himself arrested.
STYLE
::cue()

284
00:18:03,479 --> 00:18:04,480
For espionage.

285
00:18:05,147 --> 00:18:07,191
So you're asking me to get him out.

286
00:18:07,274 --> 00:18:08,526
DEPUTY DIRECTOR BAEK KITAE

287
00:18:08,609 --> 00:18:10,403
Think you could pull some strings?

288
00:18:11,153 --> 00:18:12,905
And if I do? What then?

289
00:18:15,866 --> 00:18:18,077
They won't have to announce a successor.

290
00:18:22,289 --> 00:18:24,792
And I can help my father get some rest.

291
00:18:24,875 --> 00:18:26,877
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

292
00:18:39,265 --> 00:18:43,352
BUSAN, KOREA

293
00:18:43,436 --> 00:18:45,855
[♪ classical music playing on stereo]

294
00:18:47,565 --> 00:18:50,359
[car horns honking]

295
00:18:55,531 --> 00:18:57,158
[honking continues]

296
00:18:59,702 --> 00:19:01,871
You know, I expected it
to be more chaotic.

297
00:19:02,496 --> 00:19:04,123
Heard they burned down a TV station.

298
00:19:05,124 --> 00:19:06,125
You're right.

299
00:19:06,959 --> 00:19:07,960
It is quiet.

300
00:19:08,794 --> 00:19:11,380
[Kihun] What's with the traffic?
Was there an accident?

301
00:19:12,423 --> 00:19:14,675
-[loud boom, hiss]
-[people clamoring]

302
00:19:14,759 --> 00:19:16,761
-[protester 1] Over there! They're coming!
-[Kihun] Whoa.

303
00:19:16,844 --> 00:19:19,346
-[whistles blowing]
-[Kihun] What's going on?

304
00:19:22,349 --> 00:19:24,185
[bystander exclaims]

305
00:19:24,268 --> 00:19:26,812
-[people clamoring]
-[glass shattering]

306
00:19:28,147 --> 00:19:29,440
-[car rattles]
-[Kihun] Whoa.

307
00:19:29,523 --> 00:19:30,608
[clamoring continues]

308
00:19:32,151 --> 00:19:33,235
[protester 2] Get off him!

309
00:19:34,278 --> 00:19:35,571
[Kihun] Oh, geez.

310
00:19:36,155 --> 00:19:38,532
-[clamoring continues]
-[glass breaking]

311
00:19:44,371 --> 00:19:46,248
[protester 3 crying out]

312
00:19:48,417 --> 00:19:52,004
[soldier grunts] You crazy bitch!
All right. That's it. You're dead.

313
00:19:52,087 --> 00:19:54,089
[♪ classical music continues]

314
00:20:11,649 --> 00:20:13,692
KCIA BUSAN BRANCH

315
00:20:13,776 --> 00:20:15,903
[person wailing, screaming]

316
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:21,909
-[blows landing]
-[person screaming]

317
00:20:33,838 --> 00:20:35,756
-[blows continue]
-[screaming continues]

318
00:20:37,383 --> 00:20:38,759
[agent] Hold still!

319
00:20:41,762 --> 00:20:43,347
[victim] No, please, don't!

320
00:20:44,932 --> 00:20:46,350
No, please, please!

321
00:20:46,433 --> 00:20:48,853
[groaning, screaming]

322
00:20:54,066 --> 00:20:56,026
[screaming]

323
00:20:56,110 --> 00:20:57,111
Hey!

324
00:20:57,194 --> 00:20:59,947
[victim panting, groaning]

325
00:21:00,030 --> 00:21:01,156
Sir.

326
00:21:02,157 --> 00:21:04,493
[victim panting, coughing]

327
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,787
[victims breathing heavily]

328
00:21:11,041 --> 00:21:12,960
[victims groaning, whimpering]

329
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:20,885
[grunting]
STYLE
::cue()

330
00:21:22,094 --> 00:21:24,597
[♪ jazz music playing]

331
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:28,726
Deputy Director.
I can't imagine you have much free time.

332
00:21:29,268 --> 00:21:32,855
So what brings you down to Busan, sir?

333
00:21:34,023 --> 00:21:36,191
You really don't have to be polite,
it's just us.

334
00:21:36,275 --> 00:21:37,943
The formality's uncomfortable.

335
00:21:38,611 --> 00:21:40,738
[Haksu] Well, I didn't want
to be inappropriate, sir.

336
00:21:40,821 --> 00:21:43,157
I'm just a lowly branch director general,

337
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:45,367
and you're the KCIA's second-in-command.

338
00:21:46,285 --> 00:21:48,329
So I can't really be candid unless…

339
00:21:49,038 --> 00:21:50,331
you want me to.

340
00:21:51,332 --> 00:21:52,833
And it sounds like you do?

341
00:21:54,835 --> 00:21:56,211
Don't you?

342
00:21:57,922 --> 00:21:58,923
You got a toupee?

343
00:22:00,007 --> 00:22:01,175
So you noticed?

344
00:22:01,926 --> 00:22:03,177
[laughs]

345
00:22:03,677 --> 00:22:06,055
Can't keep my damn hair for some reason.

346
00:22:07,014 --> 00:22:08,307
I think it's this job.

347
00:22:09,516 --> 00:22:10,935
Director Hwang went bald too.

348
00:22:11,018 --> 00:22:12,019
DIRECTOR GENERAL PYO HAKSU

349
00:22:12,102 --> 00:22:13,604
But you haven't.

350
00:22:15,439 --> 00:22:17,107
Why aren't you losing any?

351
00:22:17,942 --> 00:22:19,693
That'd be a question for your father.

352
00:22:20,486 --> 00:22:22,905
My old man? Right.

353
00:22:23,864 --> 00:22:25,491
What's this job got to do with it?

354
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:27,952
It's all genetics.

355
00:22:29,203 --> 00:22:31,163
Just have to get lucky at birth, I guess.

356
00:22:31,246 --> 00:22:33,457
I saw quite a scene on the drive in.

357
00:22:35,250 --> 00:22:36,377
What's the status?

358
00:22:36,460 --> 00:22:38,087
It doesn't look good.

359
00:22:38,837 --> 00:22:40,339
Masan's a wreck too.

360
00:22:42,341 --> 00:22:44,551
There's no guarantee
it won't spread to Seoul.

361
00:22:45,552 --> 00:22:47,763
Thing is, the president's
overstayed his welcome.

362
00:22:48,931 --> 00:22:52,142
You're being disrespectful.
What's your deal?

363
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:54,186
Don't you think he deserves it?

364
00:22:54,269 --> 00:22:56,188
You little shit. [clicks tongue]

365
00:22:57,523 --> 00:22:58,983
Watch your mouth.

366
00:23:00,234 --> 00:23:01,360
Yes, sir.

367
00:23:09,159 --> 00:23:10,536
[Kitae sighs]

368
00:23:13,455 --> 00:23:15,290
You've rounded up a sizable collection.

369
00:23:17,459 --> 00:23:21,296
What can I say? Commies are coming out
of the damn woodwork these days.

370
00:23:24,425 --> 00:23:26,510
Or you're creating them outta thin air.

371
00:23:28,595 --> 00:23:30,055
Well, you know how it is.

372
00:23:30,139 --> 00:23:33,726
The president needs
to see numbers to be persuaded,

373
00:23:33,809 --> 00:23:37,312
especially since he favors the MSC
over the KCIA lately.

374
00:23:37,938 --> 00:23:41,150
Those bastards just couldn't
keep their noses out of anything.

375
00:23:41,233 --> 00:23:42,234
[clicks tongue]

376
00:23:42,943 --> 00:23:44,820
You know what the hardest part is?

377
00:23:45,612 --> 00:23:47,906
You have to keep changing the narratives.

378
00:23:49,491 --> 00:23:52,036
Otherwise, people get bored
and lose interest.

379
00:23:52,119 --> 00:23:53,954
So hire a novelist or something.

380
00:23:54,038 --> 00:23:55,497
I already have, actually.

381
00:23:59,418 --> 00:24:00,461
So what is it?

382
00:24:01,336 --> 00:24:02,546
Why are you here?

383
00:24:05,257 --> 00:24:07,301
I can't get into the details.

384
00:24:09,970 --> 00:24:11,597
Here, this man.

385
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:12,931
I'm gonna need him, okay?

386
00:24:13,015 --> 00:24:14,016
HANDLER
JANG GYEONGSIK

387
00:24:14,099 --> 00:24:16,018
[all panting]

388
00:24:25,486 --> 00:24:26,653
Who's Jang Gyeongsik?

389
00:24:27,404 --> 00:24:28,405
Hold up your hand.

390
00:24:30,783 --> 00:24:32,576
[in Japanese] Who's Jang Gyeongsik?

391
00:24:33,911 --> 00:24:34,912
Raise your hand if it's you.

392
00:24:36,246 --> 00:24:37,706
-Yes?
-[in English] Get him.

393
00:24:37,790 --> 00:24:38,874
[all clamoring]

394
00:24:38,957 --> 00:24:41,794
[Kitae] Koreans born and raised in Japan
could barely understand,

395
00:24:41,877 --> 00:24:44,922
let alone resist,
South Korea's harsh anti-communist laws.

396
00:24:45,005 --> 00:24:46,256
Get the cuffs!

397
00:24:46,340 --> 00:24:48,383
[Kitae] Many of them
barely spoke Korean at all,

398
00:24:48,467 --> 00:24:52,137
which made them easy targets
in the KCIA and the MSC's quest

399
00:24:52,221 --> 00:24:55,057
to frame unsuspecting expats
for espionage.

400
00:24:55,140 --> 00:24:58,227
Catching spies brought reward money,
professional perks,

401
00:24:58,310 --> 00:25:02,064
special promotions,
even the president's personal favor.

402
00:25:02,147 --> 00:25:06,777
So, naturally, everyone in the government
became obsessed with hunting them down.

403
00:25:06,860 --> 00:25:08,362
[♪ tense music playing]

404
00:25:08,445 --> 00:25:09,822
[sobbing, sniffling]

405
00:25:10,948 --> 00:25:12,491
You want him released?

406
00:25:16,370 --> 00:25:17,621
Bold move.

407
00:25:18,247 --> 00:25:19,873
You're not worried about the director?

408
00:25:19,957 --> 00:25:21,333
Are you worried about it?

409
00:25:21,416 --> 00:25:24,753
Cho's pretty much finished, but… even so.

410
00:25:25,379 --> 00:25:26,964
Well… [sighs]

411
00:25:27,965 --> 00:25:29,925
…can you release this guy or not?

412
00:25:32,177 --> 00:25:34,972
[chuckles] You give an order, I follow it.

413
00:25:35,055 --> 00:25:37,099
I'm just a humble branch director general.

414
00:25:37,182 --> 00:25:38,600
[grunts]

415
00:25:46,275 --> 00:25:48,026
By the way,

416
00:25:48,819 --> 00:25:50,779
this stuff's all over Busan right now.

417
00:25:59,204 --> 00:26:01,665
I thought you said
you were only planning to export.

418
00:26:02,749 --> 00:26:04,585
That you wouldn't push it in Korea.
STYLE
::cue()

419
00:26:10,048 --> 00:26:12,342
-You found this here in the city?
-Mm-hmm.

420
00:26:13,510 --> 00:26:16,847
There was a woman who used to work
under Jang Geonyoung, remember her?

421
00:26:17,598 --> 00:26:18,932
Oh Yejin.

422
00:26:19,016 --> 00:26:21,685
She's a prosecutor
at the Busan District Office now.

423
00:26:21,768 --> 00:26:23,770
She's desperate to catch people
who sell that.

424
00:26:25,647 --> 00:26:28,400
Word is she's a lunatic, too.
Just like Geonyoung.

425
00:26:28,984 --> 00:26:31,320
She'll move heaven and earth
to get the job done.

426
00:26:34,865 --> 00:26:37,492
[♪ intriguing music playing]

427
00:26:37,576 --> 00:26:39,036
[dealer] Oh, yeah.

428
00:26:39,828 --> 00:26:42,748
That's the number one product
going around these days.

429
00:26:43,790 --> 00:26:46,084
Usually gets exported straight to Tokyo.

430
00:26:46,919 --> 00:26:51,215
Once you get a taste of it,
nothing else hits the same. [chuckles]

431
00:26:55,135 --> 00:26:56,386
So, uh…

432
00:26:57,387 --> 00:26:59,932
how come you're here all alone today,
Miss Oh?

433
00:27:01,642 --> 00:27:03,101
My guys are outside.

434
00:27:03,602 --> 00:27:04,895
They were just in the way.

435
00:27:06,813 --> 00:27:07,981
What about the rest?

436
00:27:10,234 --> 00:27:12,319
-How much do you need?
-[exhales]

437
00:27:12,402 --> 00:27:14,029
I need all of it.

438
00:27:14,529 --> 00:27:15,572
As much as you've got.

439
00:27:17,199 --> 00:27:18,242
[chuckles]

440
00:27:18,992 --> 00:27:20,535
I'm not sure you can handle that.

441
00:27:21,495 --> 00:27:22,579
[sighs]

442
00:27:23,664 --> 00:27:25,791
Look, are we gonna make this deal or not?

443
00:27:29,461 --> 00:27:31,588
How bad do you want it? [grunts]

444
00:27:31,672 --> 00:27:32,756
I'm up for anything.

445
00:27:34,049 --> 00:27:35,342
Yeah, me too.

446
00:27:40,973 --> 00:27:41,974
Well, come on, then.

447
00:27:42,933 --> 00:27:45,519
[laughing]

448
00:27:46,061 --> 00:27:47,688
[all laughing]

449
00:27:49,022 --> 00:27:51,900
You wanna do it now?
With the boys watching?

450
00:27:51,984 --> 00:27:53,110
Why not?

451
00:27:54,152 --> 00:27:56,405
Always better with an audience.

452
00:27:57,197 --> 00:27:59,616
Oh, wait… are you serious?

453
00:28:02,202 --> 00:28:04,621
All right. Yeah. Uh…

454
00:28:04,705 --> 00:28:06,456
[chuckling] Aw, yeah, great.

455
00:28:06,540 --> 00:28:08,667
What are you idiots looking at?
Close your eyes.

456
00:28:09,668 --> 00:28:11,003
-Right, here we go.
-[moans]

457
00:28:11,086 --> 00:28:12,587
[dealer breathing heavily]

458
00:28:12,671 --> 00:28:14,381
Wh-wh-what are you doing? Come on.

459
00:28:14,464 --> 00:28:16,216
-Don't be such a tease.
-[Yejin sighs]

460
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:18,593
[both chuckling]

461
00:28:18,677 --> 00:28:21,054
-[grunts] Come on, I can't take it!
-[moans]

462
00:28:21,138 --> 00:28:23,932
All right, let's get down to business.

463
00:28:26,810 --> 00:28:29,062
Hey! What the hell? [exclaims]

464
00:28:29,146 --> 00:28:30,939
-Goddamn it!
-[grunts]

465
00:28:31,023 --> 00:28:32,816
[both grunting]

466
00:28:32,899 --> 00:28:34,901
[♪ upbeat music playing]

467
00:28:47,080 --> 00:28:48,081
[Yejin] Come here!

468
00:28:48,749 --> 00:28:51,460
Whoa, what are you doing?
Hey, stop it! No!

469
00:28:51,543 --> 00:28:53,503
-Miss Oh, you're not allowed to--
-[gunshot]

470
00:28:56,006 --> 00:28:57,382
[dealer grunting]

471
00:29:00,052 --> 00:29:01,219
[groans]

472
00:29:02,345 --> 00:29:03,597
Who are you really?

473
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:07,350
I'm Prosecutor Oh Yejin
from the Busan District Office,

474
00:29:07,434 --> 00:29:09,603
you drug-dealing sack of shit!

475
00:29:10,228 --> 00:29:11,605
-One…
-[groaning]

476
00:29:11,688 --> 00:29:12,689
Shut up, idiot.

477
00:29:12,773 --> 00:29:13,815
-…two…
-[exclaims]

478
00:29:13,899 --> 00:29:15,192
-Cut the shit, all right?
-…three,

479
00:29:15,776 --> 00:29:18,403
-and four.
-Hey, asshole, stay down on your knees.

480
00:29:18,487 --> 00:29:20,989
Shut up. Look at me, you prick.

481
00:29:21,615 --> 00:29:23,617
Okay. Where'd you get the drugs?

482
00:29:23,700 --> 00:29:24,785
[scoffs]

483
00:29:26,244 --> 00:29:27,329
[Yejin] Listen, Kim.

484
00:29:27,412 --> 00:29:30,874
You go back to jail, you'll be doing
a mandatory minimum of ten years.

485
00:29:30,957 --> 00:29:32,667
-Understand?
-[scoffs]

486
00:29:34,211 --> 00:29:36,129
Just for pushing a little meth?

487
00:29:36,213 --> 00:29:38,548
-You're pulling my leg, aren't you?
-[chuckles]

488
00:29:38,632 --> 00:29:40,425
-Nope.
-Argh, shit!

489
00:29:40,509 --> 00:29:41,551
[groaning] Damn it!

490
00:29:41,635 --> 00:29:42,636
-You know…
-Ow.

491
00:29:42,719 --> 00:29:45,722
…I busted my ass for ten years
to become a prosecutor.

492
00:29:46,765 --> 00:29:47,974
Why?

493
00:29:48,058 --> 00:29:51,645
To throw little scumbags
like you into prison forever.

494
00:29:51,728 --> 00:29:53,480
[Kim panting]

495
00:29:54,940 --> 00:29:56,983
So I'd stake my badge on this.

496
00:29:57,651 --> 00:29:59,569
You're so screwed.

497
00:30:00,320 --> 00:30:01,738
So what's it gonna be?

498
00:30:02,447 --> 00:30:05,242
Start talking
and do a year in county jail,

499
00:30:05,325 --> 00:30:07,452
or get sent to prison for a decade?

500
00:30:07,536 --> 00:30:08,578
[grunting]

501
00:30:08,662 --> 00:30:11,081
You really wanna deal with
the other inmates every day?

502
00:30:11,164 --> 00:30:12,833
[breathing heavily]

503
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:15,836
[grunts] A year.

504
00:30:16,837 --> 00:30:19,881
-You give me your word?
-Oh, yeah, I got you.

505
00:30:19,965 --> 00:30:21,424
It's a deal then.

506
00:30:21,508 --> 00:30:23,718
So, who's supplying you?

507
00:30:26,096 --> 00:30:29,850
Changbae. He runs a lab up in Seoul.
That's where they make this stuff.

508
00:30:29,933 --> 00:30:32,394
And, man, it's, uh… just…

509
00:30:32,477 --> 00:30:34,437
It's killer. And normally they…

510
00:30:34,521 --> 00:30:38,567
they only export it to Japan, you usually
can't find it anywhere in Korea.

511
00:30:39,234 --> 00:30:41,153
But he must've needed the cash.

512
00:30:41,236 --> 00:30:43,029
So he came right to me.

513
00:30:43,113 --> 00:30:44,322
"Changbae"?

514
00:30:44,406 --> 00:30:46,533
Yeah. Park Changbae.

515
00:30:47,868 --> 00:30:49,953
[sighs] Park Changbae, huh?
STYLE
::cue()

516
00:30:51,663 --> 00:30:53,665
[humming, vocalizing]

517
00:30:53,748 --> 00:30:55,417
[♪ gentle music playing on radio]

518
00:30:55,500 --> 00:30:57,794
You're drinking before
the sun's even gone down?

519
00:30:58,378 --> 00:30:59,379
Huh?

520
00:31:00,005 --> 00:31:01,715
You know how bad that is for you?

521
00:31:04,092 --> 00:31:05,468
Come on.

522
00:31:13,268 --> 00:31:16,938
Oh, whoa, whoa, whoa. Easy.
You're breaking everything.

523
00:31:17,856 --> 00:31:19,149
-[scoffs]
-[chuckles]

524
00:31:19,232 --> 00:31:21,568
-What are you doing?
-I'd love…

525
00:31:22,903 --> 00:31:23,904
a little refill, please.

526
00:31:26,489 --> 00:31:27,616
[sighs]

527
00:31:27,699 --> 00:31:29,743
You're gonna put your stomach
through hell.

528
00:31:30,785 --> 00:31:32,746
Oh, whatever. [grunts]

529
00:31:33,288 --> 00:31:34,581
[clears throat] All right.

530
00:31:34,664 --> 00:31:36,041
[grunts]

531
00:31:37,125 --> 00:31:40,086
How about some food? Oh, what…

532
00:31:43,757 --> 00:31:45,342
What's up with you?

533
00:31:45,967 --> 00:31:47,510
Uh, what's happening?

534
00:31:48,929 --> 00:31:51,473
[chuckles] You wanna?

535
00:31:52,474 --> 00:31:53,516
What are you saying?

536
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:54,684
[chuckles]

537
00:31:55,518 --> 00:31:57,604
-What do you think? [laughing]
-Ah! Shit.

538
00:32:00,190 --> 00:32:02,692
Dumbass. Your face! [laughing]

539
00:32:04,444 --> 00:32:05,987
[gasps] Oh! Uh…

540
00:32:08,031 --> 00:32:10,992
Oh, my gosh.
I wasn't expecting you, Kitae.

541
00:32:12,285 --> 00:32:13,578
Nobody else here?

542
00:32:13,662 --> 00:32:15,497
No. We finished all the shipments,

543
00:32:15,580 --> 00:32:17,582
so everyone got to head out early.

544
00:32:18,875 --> 00:32:20,126
[door closes]

545
00:32:22,587 --> 00:32:23,755
[Kitae sighs]

546
00:32:26,091 --> 00:32:29,344
Soyeong, go get ready for the memorial.
Kihyun's going too.

547
00:32:29,427 --> 00:32:30,428
Oh.

548
00:32:31,263 --> 00:32:34,140
All right, I'll go. What about you?

549
00:32:34,224 --> 00:32:36,434
I need to talk to Changbae first.

550
00:32:43,275 --> 00:32:44,484
Okay.

551
00:32:47,445 --> 00:32:49,739
[door opens, closes]

552
00:32:50,323 --> 00:32:52,325
-[Kitae] Have a seat.
-Right, sure.

553
00:32:57,038 --> 00:32:58,290
[radio clicks off]

554
00:33:00,625 --> 00:33:01,876
[Kitae sighs]

555
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:06,881
Changbae.

556
00:33:07,465 --> 00:33:08,466
Yes, sir?

557
00:33:10,176 --> 00:33:13,888
What do you think is the most
essential virtue a person should have?

558
00:33:16,391 --> 00:33:17,434
Love, I guess?

559
00:33:18,184 --> 00:33:20,520
Love. [chuckles]

560
00:33:22,939 --> 00:33:24,983
Right, love is important, sure.

561
00:33:26,651 --> 00:33:28,153
Wanna know what I'd pick?

562
00:33:29,362 --> 00:33:31,239
Shame would be my answer.

563
00:33:32,198 --> 00:33:33,658
Shame? Really?

564
00:33:33,742 --> 00:33:36,911
There's no one I hate more
than a shameless person.

565
00:33:39,080 --> 00:33:41,708
Someone that's blithe
and careless in everything they do.

566
00:33:45,462 --> 00:33:47,630
A shameless guy is always deferent.

567
00:33:47,714 --> 00:33:51,051
He'll smile and nod
and swear he'll do anything for you.

568
00:33:51,760 --> 00:33:52,969
But when it really counts,

569
00:33:53,053 --> 00:33:55,513
he'll stick a knife in your back
like it's nothing.

570
00:33:55,597 --> 00:33:57,640
[♪ tense music playing]

571
00:33:57,724 --> 00:33:58,975
[Kitae] That's what it means…

572
00:34:02,062 --> 00:34:03,897
to be shameless in this world.

573
00:34:06,358 --> 00:34:08,026
And if you have no shame…

574
00:34:08,735 --> 00:34:11,529
you're no different
than an animal in the wild.

575
00:34:11,613 --> 00:34:12,614
Don't you think?

576
00:34:14,824 --> 00:34:16,451
[Changbae breathing shakily]

577
00:34:21,081 --> 00:34:22,540
[hammer cocks]

578
00:34:22,624 --> 00:34:24,292
You skimming our stuff?
STYLE
::cue()

579
00:34:25,710 --> 00:34:26,795
[Changbae exhales shakily]

580
00:34:27,670 --> 00:34:30,006
What? I didn't take any product.

581
00:34:30,090 --> 00:34:31,591
-[gun clicks]
-[breathing shakily]

582
00:34:32,258 --> 00:34:33,593
Look, sir, I'm sorry.

583
00:34:34,260 --> 00:34:37,430
I'm not sure we can keep working
together if you're going to do this.

584
00:34:37,514 --> 00:34:40,809
I'm telling you, I didn't do anything.
All right?

585
00:34:40,892 --> 00:34:42,685
Trust me, okay?

586
00:34:42,769 --> 00:34:44,187
Just please, don't!

587
00:34:44,270 --> 00:34:46,064
You're pushing the product in Busan.

588
00:34:46,147 --> 00:34:48,233
I didn't do that. I wouldn't betray you.

589
00:34:48,316 --> 00:34:50,318
-[gun clicks]
-[gasping]

590
00:34:50,402 --> 00:34:52,654
I didn't skim product off the top, sir.

591
00:34:54,030 --> 00:34:56,783
I didn't, I swear on my life.
Please believe me.

592
00:34:58,451 --> 00:35:00,829
[breathing shakily]

593
00:35:04,332 --> 00:35:06,084
So you're saying it wasn't you?

594
00:35:11,005 --> 00:35:12,173
[exhales shakily]

595
00:35:12,924 --> 00:35:16,428
Yes, it really wasn't me, okay?

596
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:24,728
Clean this up.

597
00:35:26,563 --> 00:35:27,647
Yes, sir. I'm on it.

598
00:35:30,567 --> 00:35:32,652
MILITARY SECURITY COMMAND

599
00:35:32,736 --> 00:35:34,738
[typewriter keys clacking]

600
00:35:54,966 --> 00:35:56,843
-Wanna have a cigarette?
-Sure, sir.

601
00:36:00,513 --> 00:36:01,681
[grunts]

602
00:36:05,143 --> 00:36:06,186
Mmm.

603
00:36:07,771 --> 00:36:09,063
-Mmm, mmm.
-Thanks.

604
00:36:14,110 --> 00:36:16,070
How's the office? Settling in?

605
00:36:16,654 --> 00:36:18,323
Yes, sir. It's perfect.

606
00:36:18,406 --> 00:36:20,909
It was just yesterday you were a captain,

607
00:36:20,992 --> 00:36:23,620
and now you've already
been promoted again. Wow.

608
00:36:23,703 --> 00:36:25,038
Time really flies.

609
00:36:25,705 --> 00:36:28,792
-Well, you played a big part in that.
-Oh, come on, that's not true.

610
00:36:29,501 --> 00:36:30,919
You earned it all yourself.

611
00:36:31,002 --> 00:36:33,004
I don't know… [chuckles]

612
00:36:33,546 --> 00:36:35,924
Didn't you say
you had a memorial service today?

613
00:36:36,716 --> 00:36:37,884
Yes, sir. For my father.

614
00:36:37,967 --> 00:36:41,012
[clicks tongue] Wrap up and head out.
Why are you still working?

615
00:36:41,596 --> 00:36:45,058
I have a few more things to take care of.
I'll go once I'm finished.

616
00:36:47,393 --> 00:36:48,895
I imagine you'll be

617
00:36:49,729 --> 00:36:51,940
seeing your brother, right?

618
00:36:54,025 --> 00:36:56,402
-Yes, sir.
-[chuckles]

619
00:36:56,486 --> 00:36:58,696
The Busan situation… [licks lips]

620
00:36:58,780 --> 00:37:01,115
…must keep him pretty busy, huh?

621
00:37:03,117 --> 00:37:05,870
Well, I suppose so.

622
00:37:40,864 --> 00:37:41,865
[Kitae] Here.

623
00:37:48,788 --> 00:37:49,789
To your promotion.

624
00:37:49,873 --> 00:37:51,457
-Thank you so much.
-[Soyeong chuckles softly]

625
00:37:54,419 --> 00:37:57,964
Our Kihyun's a big man now, huh?
Lieutenant colonel already.

626
00:37:58,047 --> 00:37:59,757
None of your classmates can say that.
STYLE
::cue()

627
00:38:00,341 --> 00:38:02,719
Before you know it,
he'll be a general, don't you think?

628
00:38:03,303 --> 00:38:05,388
-It's all because of you.
-Oh, please.

629
00:38:05,471 --> 00:38:07,765
No, I barely lifted a finger. [chuckles]

630
00:38:11,269 --> 00:38:14,522
You know, Kihyun, Kitae pulled
a lot of strings behind the scenes.

631
00:38:15,523 --> 00:38:18,109
We owe everything we have to him,
you know.

632
00:38:18,192 --> 00:38:20,278
This beautiful home, for instance.

633
00:38:20,361 --> 00:38:22,363
You should really come by more often.

634
00:38:22,447 --> 00:38:24,240
-We would love to have you--
-Soyeong.

635
00:38:24,782 --> 00:38:26,200
Your food's getting cold.

636
00:38:29,787 --> 00:38:31,289
Come on, aren't you gonna eat with us?

637
00:38:31,915 --> 00:38:34,042
Do I have to keep feeding you like a baby?

638
00:38:34,125 --> 00:38:36,836
-Say "ah."
-No, I'm too tired right now.

639
00:38:37,754 --> 00:38:40,757
If you finish your dinner,
I'll read you a bedtime story later.

640
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:41,966
Come on.

641
00:38:43,718 --> 00:38:47,847
Uncle Kihyun, I don't know
what a promotion is.

642
00:38:48,723 --> 00:38:51,059
Hmm. It means I moved up in rank.

643
00:38:51,142 --> 00:38:52,477
I'm a lieutenant colonel now.

644
00:38:52,560 --> 00:38:54,395
What's "rank"?

645
00:38:54,479 --> 00:38:58,316
Well, uh, you moved up
from first grade to second grade, right?

646
00:38:58,399 --> 00:38:59,400
It's like that.

647
00:39:00,568 --> 00:39:04,822
-Oh, so you went up higher?
-Mm-hmm.

648
00:39:04,906 --> 00:39:09,869
Is Uncle Kitae more higher up than you,
or are you more higher up than him now?

649
00:39:09,953 --> 00:39:12,538
[chuckles] He's much higher up than me.

650
00:39:14,749 --> 00:39:17,627
General Hwang been good to you?
Now that you're working for him?

651
00:39:17,710 --> 00:39:18,836
Yes.

652
00:39:18,920 --> 00:39:21,047
Not giving you a hard time
because we're related?

653
00:39:21,673 --> 00:39:22,674
Nobody is.

654
00:39:22,757 --> 00:39:24,759
The colonel's been good to me too.
So, it's been fine.

655
00:39:25,969 --> 00:39:28,221
Ahn Jaeho, right?
Military Academy graduate.

656
00:39:28,304 --> 00:39:29,430
Yes.

657
00:39:31,140 --> 00:39:33,184
I hear
that he's General Hwang's right-hand.

658
00:39:33,851 --> 00:39:35,061
He mention me at all?

659
00:39:36,354 --> 00:39:37,772
I don't believe he has.

660
00:39:38,815 --> 00:39:41,985
Word is Hwang's been
gathering officers around him lately.

661
00:39:43,236 --> 00:39:45,488
[Kihyun] He mostly meets with colonels
from the academy.

662
00:39:45,571 --> 00:39:46,781
They drink, play golf.

663
00:39:46,864 --> 00:39:50,284
He's made it clear he's a strong leader,
so lots of people follow him.

664
00:39:52,078 --> 00:39:53,997
Just keep an eye on him, you got that?

665
00:39:55,081 --> 00:39:57,750
Watch who joins his group
and track all his people.

666
00:40:00,336 --> 00:40:01,337
Are you not…

667
00:40:02,088 --> 00:40:03,172
comfortable with that?

668
00:40:04,924 --> 00:40:06,092
No, I'm fine.

669
00:40:08,428 --> 00:40:09,554
Kihyun, look.

670
00:40:10,805 --> 00:40:13,266
You're my brother, hmm?

671
00:40:14,392 --> 00:40:16,519
You know you can't be
in General Hwang's circle.

672
00:40:18,271 --> 00:40:19,605
Of course. I'm aware.

673
00:40:23,067 --> 00:40:26,779
Sorry, but,
who's General Hwang, Uncle Kihyun?

674
00:40:26,863 --> 00:40:28,072
[Kihyun chuckles]

675
00:40:28,156 --> 00:40:30,533
[phone ringing]

676
00:40:34,829 --> 00:40:35,830
Yes, hello?

677
00:40:36,914 --> 00:40:39,542
-A few more bites. Here.
-Just a minute.

678
00:40:40,293 --> 00:40:42,462
Sorry, but it's Miss Choi.

679
00:40:46,382 --> 00:40:48,843
-I'll take it downstairs.
-[Soyeong] Mmm.

680
00:41:07,528 --> 00:41:08,529
Hi.

681
00:41:08,613 --> 00:41:10,490
How did it go with Professor Jang?

682
00:41:10,573 --> 00:41:11,574
Hold on a minute.

683
00:41:12,200 --> 00:41:14,243
Soyeong, hang up.

684
00:41:16,537 --> 00:41:18,247
-[clears throat]
-[phone cradle clicks]

685
00:41:19,248 --> 00:41:20,333
We leave tomorrow.

686
00:41:20,875 --> 00:41:23,002
Do you have everything ready?

687
00:41:24,128 --> 00:41:25,546
Don't worry about that.

688
00:41:26,255 --> 00:41:28,216
I just need you to make it on time.

689
00:41:28,716 --> 00:41:30,426
[♪ intriguing music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

690
00:41:52,573 --> 00:41:53,908
[Ikeda exhales]

691
00:41:55,284 --> 00:41:56,285
[in Japanese] Father.

692
00:41:57,578 --> 00:42:00,623
As for your successor,
have you decided yet?

693
00:42:06,671 --> 00:42:08,548
It's Kimura, isn't it?

694
00:42:14,679 --> 00:42:15,888
So,

695
00:42:15,972 --> 00:42:19,142
you want me to step aside, too,
is that right?

696
00:42:23,396 --> 00:42:24,689
[sighs]

697
00:42:26,524 --> 00:42:28,985
No matter who the successor is,

698
00:42:29,777 --> 00:42:32,280
I still can't leave things to you all yet.

699
00:42:35,533 --> 00:42:37,660
So keep supporting me

700
00:42:37,743 --> 00:42:40,621
and learning from me, hmm?

701
00:42:40,705 --> 00:42:42,957
Stay here, by my side…

702
00:42:46,294 --> 00:42:48,713
the same way you always have.

703
00:42:49,672 --> 00:42:50,965
Hmm?

704
00:42:54,177 --> 00:42:55,386
[Yuji chuckles softly]

705
00:42:57,263 --> 00:42:58,681
Yes, I promise.

706
00:42:59,599 --> 00:43:01,893
I'll always do whatever you tell me.

707
00:43:01,976 --> 00:43:03,060
[Ikeda] Uh-huh.

708
00:43:07,148 --> 00:43:08,482
I'll go get some tea.

709
00:43:09,275 --> 00:43:11,319
Oh, sure. [chuckles]

710
00:43:21,662 --> 00:43:22,997
[exhales deeply]

711
00:43:24,165 --> 00:43:26,125
-[bell chimes]
-[monks chanting]

712
00:43:26,209 --> 00:43:27,543
[Kitae] As fate would have it,

713
00:43:27,627 --> 00:43:30,922
Chairman Ikeda died of cardiac arrest
at his residence that night.

714
00:43:31,005 --> 00:43:32,632
[chanting continues]

715
00:43:34,842 --> 00:43:37,678
[Kitae] Yakuza from all across Japan
attended the funeral.

716
00:43:38,304 --> 00:43:41,515
And since the chairman died
without naming a successor,

717
00:43:41,599 --> 00:43:43,976
speculation over
who would fill the power vacuum

718
00:43:44,060 --> 00:43:46,604
became the center
of the mourners' attention.

719
00:43:50,316 --> 00:43:51,734
[chanting continues in distance]

720
00:43:56,697 --> 00:43:57,823
[grunts softly]

721
00:44:04,080 --> 00:44:05,164
Okay, Professor.

722
00:44:06,040 --> 00:44:08,834
Everything you saw in Korea?
Forget about it.

723
00:44:10,086 --> 00:44:11,629
Erase it, you understand?

724
00:44:16,425 --> 00:44:17,635
[in Japanese] And why don't you…

725
00:44:18,469 --> 00:44:20,554
put in a good word with Harimoto
while you're at it.

726
00:44:44,996 --> 00:44:46,998
[♪ somber music playing]

727
00:44:51,836 --> 00:44:53,212
[bell chimes]

728
00:44:57,174 --> 00:44:58,384
[bell chimes]

729
00:45:13,649 --> 00:45:14,900
[bell chimes]
STYLE
::cue()

730
00:45:19,530 --> 00:45:21,115
[bell chimes]

731
00:45:22,700 --> 00:45:24,118
[camera shutters clicking]

732
00:45:38,883 --> 00:45:41,802
That's enough! No more photos.

733
00:46:02,114 --> 00:46:04,742
[crows cawing]

734
00:46:12,625 --> 00:46:13,751
[Kitae, in Korean] In the end,

735
00:46:13,834 --> 00:46:16,712
the Ikeda clan decided
to choose the next kumicho by vote.

736
00:46:17,588 --> 00:46:20,716
Choi Yuji secured nine votes
out of the gate.

737
00:46:21,425 --> 00:46:25,179
The question is will Harimoto stand by her
like he promised?

738
00:46:25,888 --> 00:46:28,849
If so, the position would finally be hers.

739
00:46:41,028 --> 00:46:43,114
[moderator, in Japanese]
The voting process is complete.

740
00:46:43,823 --> 00:46:45,825
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

741
00:46:46,992 --> 00:46:49,078
We will now count the ballots.

742
00:46:54,208 --> 00:46:56,502
[in Korean] It's time.
They're counting ballots.

743
00:47:05,428 --> 00:47:06,429
"Ikeda Yuji."

744
00:47:13,310 --> 00:47:14,311
"Kimura Yoichi."

745
00:47:17,606 --> 00:47:18,607
"Kimura Yoichi."

746
00:47:24,572 --> 00:47:25,573
"Ikeda Yuji."

747
00:47:29,076 --> 00:47:30,369
"Kimura Yoichi."

748
00:47:33,080 --> 00:47:34,248
"Ikeda Yuji."

749
00:47:38,335 --> 00:47:39,420
"Kimura Yoichi."

750
00:47:43,257 --> 00:47:44,258
"Ikeda Yuji."

751
00:47:48,679 --> 00:47:49,680
"Ikeda Yuji."

752
00:47:51,348 --> 00:47:52,349
"Kimura Yoichi."

753
00:47:54,685 --> 00:47:55,686
"Kimura Yoichi."

754
00:47:58,772 --> 00:47:59,773
"Ikeda Yuji."

755
00:48:03,068 --> 00:48:04,069
"Kimura Yoichi."

756
00:48:06,530 --> 00:48:07,573
"Ikeda Yuji."

757
00:48:10,242 --> 00:48:11,577
"Ikeda Yuji."

758
00:48:11,660 --> 00:48:14,747
IKEDA YUJI - KIMURA YOICHI

759
00:48:18,542 --> 00:48:19,877
"Kimura Yoichi."

760
00:48:26,175 --> 00:48:28,469
Kimura Yoichi, ten votes.

761
00:48:29,094 --> 00:48:31,096
Ikeda Yuji, nine votes.

762
00:48:31,722 --> 00:48:33,432
Nineteen votes in total.

763
00:48:33,516 --> 00:48:34,683
According to these results,

764
00:48:34,767 --> 00:48:38,312
Kimura Yoichi is hereby named
the fourth kumicho of the Ikeda clan.

765
00:48:38,395 --> 00:48:40,189
[applause]
STYLE
::cue()

766
00:49:07,550 --> 00:49:10,344
[Kimura] How dare
this Korean mongrel whore…

767
00:49:11,303 --> 00:49:13,889
aim to take full control of our clan.

768
00:49:15,140 --> 00:49:17,560
Go on, drag her out of here before I do.

769
00:49:18,894 --> 00:49:20,896
[♪ tense music playing]

770
00:49:53,345 --> 00:49:54,430
[grunts softly]

771
00:50:13,991 --> 00:50:15,075
[exhales]

772
00:50:17,077 --> 00:50:18,162
[gulps]

773
00:50:30,716 --> 00:50:31,884
[grunts softly]

774
00:50:34,011 --> 00:50:36,305
[coughing]

775
00:50:51,737 --> 00:50:54,073
You bitch! What'd you…

776
00:50:54,156 --> 00:50:56,075
[grunts, splutters]

777
00:50:58,661 --> 00:51:00,371
[gasping]

778
00:51:01,580 --> 00:51:03,165
[groaning]

779
00:51:05,084 --> 00:51:08,045
[whimpering, coughing]

780
00:51:11,256 --> 00:51:13,384
Yuji! Yuji!

781
00:51:13,467 --> 00:51:15,302
[coughing]

782
00:51:15,386 --> 00:51:16,679
[grunting]

783
00:51:16,762 --> 00:51:19,098
-[water splashing]
-[continues coughing]

784
00:51:20,808 --> 00:51:22,101
Yuji!

785
00:51:25,312 --> 00:51:26,980
Yuji…

786
00:51:27,064 --> 00:51:29,066
[♪ dramatic music playing]

787
00:51:45,165 --> 00:51:47,251
-[hammer cocks]
-[breathing heavily]

788
00:51:48,794 --> 00:51:50,379
[yakuza member gasping]

789
00:51:52,131 --> 00:51:54,007
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

790
00:52:10,691 --> 00:52:13,026
[Kimura gasping, wheezing]

791
00:52:20,701 --> 00:52:21,869
[Yuji grunts]

792
00:52:33,130 --> 00:52:34,965
Listen, I'm kumicho now.

793
00:52:36,383 --> 00:52:37,551
Are there any objections?

794
00:52:39,303 --> 00:52:41,013
[all] We submit to you!
STYLE
::cue()

795
00:52:43,182 --> 00:52:46,518
OCTOBER 26, 1979

796
00:52:46,602 --> 00:52:49,104
[Kitae, in Korean] Meanwhile,
there was another group gathering

797
00:52:49,188 --> 00:52:51,732
with their eyes
on their own kumicho's seat.

798
00:52:51,815 --> 00:52:53,108
[slurps]

799
00:52:54,985 --> 00:52:58,030
Hey, slow down. Quit drinking so much.

800
00:52:59,907 --> 00:53:01,950
Director Cho, did you make it to Busan?

801
00:53:03,660 --> 00:53:05,245
What did you find out about the protests?

802
00:53:05,329 --> 00:53:08,081
It's just… students and normal people.

803
00:53:08,165 --> 00:53:09,625
[chopsticks clatter]

804
00:53:09,708 --> 00:53:11,502
They burned down a broadcasting station.

805
00:53:12,169 --> 00:53:13,754
They're not just normal people.

806
00:53:15,172 --> 00:53:16,965
[clears throat] Sir, listen.

807
00:53:17,716 --> 00:53:21,595
We'd better take drastic measures
before these protests get worse.

808
00:53:21,678 --> 00:53:24,473
This is no time to be talking
about martial law.

809
00:53:24,556 --> 00:53:27,810
Busan and Masan aren't islands.
Who says it won't spread to the capital?

810
00:53:27,893 --> 00:53:29,812
I know that! [clicks tongue]

811
00:53:30,562 --> 00:53:31,855
That's why we need to crush them!

812
00:53:31,939 --> 00:53:34,525
In Cambodia,
they killed three million people!

813
00:53:35,108 --> 00:53:37,152
If we roll armor
over a couple million Reds,

814
00:53:37,236 --> 00:53:38,612
would anyone care?

815
00:53:39,321 --> 00:53:40,322
[sighs]

816
00:53:41,573 --> 00:53:44,493
[Cho] You crazy son of a bitch,
I'm sick of your bullshit.

817
00:53:44,576 --> 00:53:45,744
What?

818
00:53:48,038 --> 00:53:49,081
[glass thuds]

819
00:53:50,707 --> 00:53:52,000
You damn lunatic.

820
00:53:52,835 --> 00:53:55,921
Keep talking like that
and you'll be the first to die.

821
00:53:56,004 --> 00:53:58,298
-You little…
-[glass thuds]

822
00:53:58,382 --> 00:54:00,384
[♪ tense music playing]

823
00:54:01,885 --> 00:54:04,596
Director Cho, explain yourself.

824
00:54:04,680 --> 00:54:05,681
Sir, listen.

825
00:54:06,974 --> 00:54:09,226
The more you keep scum like this
by your side,

826
00:54:09,309 --> 00:54:11,270
the sooner this country collapses.

827
00:54:11,854 --> 00:54:12,855
What?

828
00:54:13,438 --> 00:54:15,357
The good of our people should come first.

829
00:54:19,611 --> 00:54:21,321
[cigarette sizzles]

830
00:54:24,366 --> 00:54:25,409
Look at me.

831
00:54:26,743 --> 00:54:27,953
You wanna be shot?

832
00:54:37,170 --> 00:54:38,630
[knock on door]

833
00:54:38,714 --> 00:54:39,923
[door opens]

834
00:54:44,177 --> 00:54:45,178
You have a call, sir.

835
00:54:49,683 --> 00:54:50,684
[door closes]

836
00:55:01,403 --> 00:55:02,446
[sighs]

837
00:55:04,406 --> 00:55:05,407
[Kitae] Sir.

838
00:55:05,991 --> 00:55:07,909
Choi Yuji just made herself the kumicho.

839
00:55:08,452 --> 00:55:10,787
It's not the time for that.
You need to get over here.

840
00:55:11,580 --> 00:55:13,540
I've got a bad feeling.

841
00:55:13,624 --> 00:55:15,917
[rain pattering]

842
00:55:16,001 --> 00:55:19,171
Cho might be about
to pull something tonight.

843
00:55:19,254 --> 00:55:20,505
Get here now.

844
00:55:22,257 --> 00:55:23,425
I'm on my way.

845
00:55:24,259 --> 00:55:25,260
[phone cradle clicks]

846
00:55:32,017 --> 00:55:33,185
Gungjeong-dong. Now.

847
00:55:33,268 --> 00:55:35,270
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

848
00:55:43,779 --> 00:55:46,114
[clears throat, exhales]

849
00:55:52,245 --> 00:55:53,497
[gunshots]

850
00:55:54,289 --> 00:55:57,292
-Oh, shit. What the hell?
-[Kihun] Wh-what was that?

851
00:55:58,251 --> 00:56:00,128
[gunfire]

852
00:56:00,212 --> 00:56:02,339
-[Kihun gasps]
-[gunfire continues]

853
00:56:07,594 --> 00:56:08,762
Wait, sir, be careful.

854
00:56:28,156 --> 00:56:30,200
Damn it! Ah, shit.
STYLE
::cue()

855
00:56:31,243 --> 00:56:32,244
Director.

856
00:56:32,327 --> 00:56:34,579
-[gun clicking]
-[Cho] Son of a bitch!

857
00:56:34,663 --> 00:56:36,456
Hey! Bring me your gun!

858
00:56:37,416 --> 00:56:38,917
Ah, shit, come on!

859
00:56:40,001 --> 00:56:41,878
The fucking thing's jammed!

860
00:56:43,422 --> 00:56:46,383
Hey, why are all the lights out?

861
00:56:46,466 --> 00:56:47,467
Sir?

862
00:56:48,427 --> 00:56:50,721
It's pitch black.
How am I supposed to do this?

863
00:56:51,388 --> 00:56:52,764
Please, tell me what's happening, sir.

864
00:56:53,807 --> 00:56:55,142
Stay outside.

865
00:56:55,225 --> 00:56:57,185
I'm gonna finish this once and for all.

866
00:56:59,062 --> 00:57:00,188
Damn it.

867
00:57:04,901 --> 00:57:07,320
Sir, uh… wh-what the hell's happening?

868
00:57:07,988 --> 00:57:10,532
Beats me,
but whatever it is, we're screwed.

869
00:57:12,784 --> 00:57:14,578
-[gunshot]
-[Kihun gasping]

870
00:57:15,829 --> 00:57:16,997
Shit.

871
00:57:19,082 --> 00:57:20,250
[gunshot]

872
00:57:22,294 --> 00:57:25,005
On October 26th, 1979,

873
00:57:25,088 --> 00:57:28,675
the kumicho, the boss,
the president of South Korea,

874
00:57:28,759 --> 00:57:29,926
died.

875
00:57:30,010 --> 00:57:32,012
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

